1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,406
A favourite question.

2
00:00:01,406 --> 00:00:12,070
A linear molecule cut at three sites gives four pieces; a circular plasmid cut at three sites gives only three, because a ring has no ends.

3
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:18,815
Either way, the fragment sizes must add back up to the whole molecule, twelve kilobases here.

4
00:00:18,815 --> 00:00:23,763
And two fragments of the same size run together as one brighter band.

